<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=cinematograph">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cinematograph</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1892">1892</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as kinematograph, Cinématographe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The cinematograph is an early motion-picture machine that served as both film camera and projector; the French inventor Léon Bouly coined the name in a patent of 12 February 1892, and filed for a version that could also project in December 1893. The Lumière brothers filed a patent for their machine, which could also print films, on 13 February 1895, and Louis Lumière first presented a film in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 22 March 1895. After their public screening in December 1895 it became a popular attraction across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cinematograph.jpg" alt="Cinematograph" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcellin Auzolle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cinematographe_Lumiere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1892</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>France</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Léon Bouly · Lumière brothers</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The Lumière brothers’ machine of 1895 gave the famous early screenings in Paris; the first commercial screening of films took place in New York in May 1895.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/photography">Photography<span>1826–1827</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=cinematograph">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
